%% seq_02_task_crud.mmd
%% Updated 2026-06-26 (verified).
%% Reader intent: See the main task interaction families together before entering create/update, status/assignment, or delete specifics.
%% Key boundary: Overview keeps one sequence per capability block and leaves validation nuances and branch-heavy logic to detail diagrams.
%% Current caveat: Task workflow and assignment are tightly coupled at runtime, so this overview keeps them adjacent even though separate commands/routes are involved.

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as User
    participant B as Browser
    participant C as Controller
    participant Factory as Action Factory
    participant Cmd as Command
    participant Repo as Repository
    participant Evt as Event Bus

    Note over U, Evt: CREATE OR UPDATE TASK
    U->>B: Submit task form
    B->>C: POST/PUT /tasks
    C->>Factory: makeCreateTaskCommand(externalDeps, notificationPublicApi)
    Factory->>Cmd: CreateTaskCommand(execCtx, extDeps, notifApi, cache)
    Cmd->>Repo: Persist task aggregate
    Cmd->>Evt: Emit task:created or task:updated
    C-->>B: Redirect to task page

    Note over U, Evt: EXECUTE TASK WORKFLOW
    U->>B: Change status or assign assignee
    B->>C: PUT /tasks/:id or /tasks/:id/status
    C->>Factory: makeUpdateTaskStatusCommand(extDeps, notificationPublicApi)
    Factory->>Cmd: UpdateTaskStatusCommand(execCtx, extDeps, notifApi, cache)
    Cmd->>Repo: Save task state
    Cmd->>Evt: Emit task:assigned or task:status:changed
    C-->>B: Return updated task

    Note over U, Evt: DELETE TASK
    U->>B: Delete task
    B->>C: DELETE /tasks/:id
    C->>Factory: makeDeleteTaskCommand(extDeps, notificationPublicApi)
    Factory->>Cmd: DeleteTaskCommand(execCtx, extDeps, notifApi, cache)
    Cmd->>Repo: Soft delete task
    Cmd->>Evt: Emit task:deleted
    C-->>B: Redirect to list
